1.1.text:
Article 2

The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence are:
a. to prevent all forms of violence against women and children;
b. to provide protection and services to women and children victims of gender-based violence;

c. to provide a sense of security to women and children victims of violence;
d. to restore the physical, psychological and economic condition of women and children victims of violence;

e. the best interests of women and children victims of violence that occur in the domestic and/or public sphere; and

f. to provide certainty of assistance to the victim in the legal process against perpetrators of violence against women and children.

Article 18

(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17 shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:

a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population and civil registration;
f. law;
g. women's empowerment and child protection;
h. cooperatives and micro enterprises;
i. mental and spiritual affairs; and
j. peace and order.
k. Community and pekon empowerment
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 17

(1) To prevent acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government shall carry out empowerment and build awareness among families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall carry out the following efforts:

a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in formal, non-formal, and informal education;
b. providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income improvement and social services;

BAGIAN HUKUM SETDA KABUPATEN PESISIR BARAT

c. creating a friendly and safe work environment atmosphere for women;

d. building community participation and concern for the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. building and providing an easily accessible information system; f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children.

Article 3

The scope of regulation in the Protection of Women and Children from acts of violence includes:

a. Forms of violence against women and children; b. Rights of victims;
c. Obligations and responsibilities;
d. Implementation of protection;
e. Cooperation and partnership;
f. Assistance;
g. Child-friendly regency;
h. Funding.

LEGAL DIVISION SETDA PESISIR BARAT REGENCY

Article 29

(1) Funding for protection of women and children victims of violence includes:

a. medical services, which include doctor's examinations, treatment costs, hospital costs, medicine costs and medical support costs;
b. medicolegal services, which include examinations for Visum et Repertum and Visum et Psikiatrikum;
c. psychosocial services, consisting of counseling and psychological therapy as well as safe houses (shelters);
d. legal services;
e. economic empowerment, in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access.
(2) Fund management is carried out through technical institutions designated by the Regional Government and conducted in a transparent manner and legally accountable.

Article 14

(1) Obligations and responsibilities of Regional Government as referred to in Article 13 letter a include:

a. establishing policies for protection, empowerment of women and children;
b. implementing policies, protection, and empowerment of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children;
e. allocating budgets for the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children, in accordance with regional financial capacity;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection and empowerment of women and children; and
g. realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.
(2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and action activities for protection and empowerment of women and children in the Regional Action Plan as a basis for Regional Apparatuses in implementing protection and empowerment of women and children.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2) is part of the RPJMD.
(4) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), are regulated by Regent Regulation.

LEGAL DIVISION SETDA PESISIR BARAT REGENCY

Article 7

(1) Sexual violence as referred to in Article 4 letter c includes: a. non-physical sexual harassment;

b. physical sexual harassment;

c. forced contraception;

d. forced sterilization;

e. forced marriage;

f. sexual torture;

g. sexual exploitation;

h. sexual slavery; and

i. electronic-based sexual violence

(2) In addition to Sexual Violence Crimes as referred to in paragraph (1), Sexual Violence Crimes also include:

a. rape;
b. indecent acts;
c. intercourse with Children, indecent acts against Children, and/or sexual exploitation of Children;

LEGAL DIVISION SETDA PESISIR BARAT REGENCY

d. acts violating decency that are contrary to the victim's will and religious values recognized in Indonesia;

e. pornography involving Children or pornography that explicitly contains violence and sexual exploitation;

f. forced prostitution;

g. criminal acts of human trafficking aimed at sexual exploitation;

h. sexual violence within the household;

i. criminal acts of money laundering where the predicate crime is a Sexual Violence Crime; and

j. other criminal acts explicitly stated as Sexual Violence Crimes as regulated in the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 11

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights:

a. the right to be respected in dignity and worth as human beings; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling in an appropriate, comfortable, and needs-based manner;
h. the right of victims and their families to receive facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and
j. to receive continuous handling until the rehabilitation stage.

