d. neglect;

e. exploitation; and/or

f. other violence.

3.2.text:
Article 18

(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17 shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:

a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population and civil registration;
f. law;
g. women's empowerment and child protection;
h. cooperatives and micro enterprises;
i. mental and spiritual affairs; and
j. peace and order.
k. Community and pekon empowerment
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 26

(1) Assistance includes all integrated efforts to restore and strengthen the condition of victims, carried out by health workers, education, police, prosecutors, courts, advocates, social workers, companion volunteers and spiritual advisors.

(2) Assistance as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(3) The duties of assistants are:

a. providing sufficient information to victims about their rights; b. providing psychosocial services to victims so that victims feel safe and comfortable;
c. accompanying victims during the medical examination and recovery process; d. accompanying victims during the medicolegal process;
e. accompanying victims during the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
f. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
g. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;
h. coordinating with other assistants; and
i. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

Article 2

The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence are:
a. to prevent all forms of violence against women and children;
b. to provide protection and services to women and children victims of gender-based violence;

c. to provide a sense of security to women and children victims of violence;
d. to restore the physical, psychological and economic condition of women and children victims of violence;

e. the best interests of women and children victims of violence that occur in the domestic and/or public sphere; and

f. to provide certainty of assistance to the victim in the legal process against perpetrators of violence against women and children.

Article 19

(1) In order to provide protection services to women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government shall establish UPTD PPA. (2) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1), functions to implement services:

a. community complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) Further provisions regarding the organization and working procedures of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation.

BAGIAN HUKUM SETDA KABUPATEN PESISIR BARAT

(4) To assist in the protection of women and children, the Regional Government may establish:

a. Task Force for the Prevention and Handling of Trafficking in Persons Crimes;
b. Task Force for the Prevention of Child Marriage;
c. Task Force for Child-Friendly Regency or other designation; d. Regional Action Committee for the elimination of the worst forms of child labor;
e. Pesisir Barat Regional Children's Forum;
f. Community-Based Integrated Child Protection (PATBM).

Article 24

(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children, cooperation may be carried out with:

a. Central Government;
b. Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments;
d. Non-Governmental Organizations;
e. Community;
f. Higher Education Institutions; and
g. Mass Media.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. recovery of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration;
d. provision of evidence and witnesses; and
e. followed up in accordance with applicable law.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of a Cooperation Agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 29

(1) Funding for protection of women and children victims of violence includes:

a. medical services, which include doctor's examinations, treatment costs, hospital costs, medicine costs and medical support costs;
b. medicolegal services, which include examinations for Visum et Repertum and Visum et Psikiatrikum;
c. psychosocial services, consisting of counseling and psychological therapy as well as safe houses (shelters);
d. legal services;
e. economic empowerment, in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access.
(2) Fund management is carried out through technical institutions designated by the Regional Government and conducted in a transparent manner and legally accountable.

