Article 17

(1) To prevent acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government shall carry out empowerment and build awareness among families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall carry out the following efforts:

a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in formal, non-formal, and informal education;
b. providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income improvement and social services;

BAGIAN HUKUM SETDA KABUPATEN PESISIR BARAT

c. creating a friendly and safe work environment atmosphere for women;

d. building community participation and concern for the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. building and providing an easily accessible information system; f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children.

Article 26

(1) Assistance includes all integrated efforts to restore and strengthen the condition of victims, carried out by health workers, education, police, prosecutors, courts, advocates, social workers, companion volunteers and spiritual advisors.

(2) Assistance as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(3) The duties of assistants are:

a. providing sufficient information to victims about their rights; b. providing psychosocial services to victims so that victims feel safe and comfortable;
c. accompanying victims during the medical examination and recovery process; d. accompanying victims during the medicolegal process;
e. accompanying victims during the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
f. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
g. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;
h. coordinating with other assistants; and
i. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

Article 27

(1) In the framework of implementing the Convention on the Rights of the Child and various laws and regulations as well as policies related to the fulfillment of children's rights and special protection of children, the Regional Government, Private Sector and Community Institutions make efforts to realize a Child-Friendly Regency.

(2) To realize a Child-Friendly Regency as referred to in paragraph (1), child-friendly sub-districts and child-friendly villages/urban villages must be established.

(3) The Regional Government, Private Sector and Community Institutions incorporated in the Task Force in realizing a child-friendly regency must pay attention to children's rights relating to the rights to life, growth and development, protection and participation

LEGAL DIVISION REGIONAL SECRETARIAT OF WEST PESISIR REGENCY

(4) The Child-Friendly Regency Task Force as referred to in paragraph (3) is responsible for the fulfillment of children's rights relating to: a. civil rights and freedoms;

b. family environment and alternative care;

c. basic health and welfare;

d. education, utilization of leisure time and cultural arts activities; e. special protection of children.

(5) Further provisions regarding Child-Friendly Regency, child-friendly sub-districts and child-friendly villages/urban villages are regulated in a Regent Regulation.

Article 19

(1) In order to provide protection services to women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government shall establish UPTD PPA. (2) UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1), functions to implement services:

a. community complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) Further provisions regarding the organization and working procedures of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation.

BAGIAN HUKUM SETDA KABUPATEN PESISIR BARAT

(4) To assist in the protection of women and children, the Regional Government may establish:

a. Task Force for the Prevention and Handling of Trafficking in Persons Crimes;
b. Task Force for the Prevention of Child Marriage;
c. Task Force for Child-Friendly Regency or other designation; d. Regional Action Committee for the elimination of the worst forms of child labor;
e. Pesisir Barat Regional Children's Forum;
f. Community-Based Integrated Child Protection (PATBM).

Article 18

(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17 shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:

a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population and civil registration;
f. law;
g. women's empowerment and child protection;
h. cooperatives and micro enterprises;
i. mental and spiritual affairs; and
j. peace and order.
k. Community and pekon empowerment
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out in an integrated and sustainable manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 30

(1) Officials who do not carry out their obligations and responsibilities as referred to in Article 14, shall be subject to administrative actions and/or sanctions.

(2) Administrative actions and/or sanctions as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:

a. Verbal reprimand;
b. Written reprimand;

LEGAL DIVISION REGIONAL SECRETARIAT OF WEST PESISIR REGENCY

c. Written statement of dissatisfaction;

d. Deduction of performance allowance by 25% (twenty-five percent) for 12 months.

(3) The officials referred to in paragraph (1) are the Head of the PPPAKB Office or those in charge of the protection of women and children.

Article 2

The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence are:
a. to prevent all forms of violence against women and children;
b. to provide protection and services to women and children victims of gender-based violence;

c. to provide a sense of security to women and children victims of violence;
d. to restore the physical, psychological and economic condition of women and children victims of violence;

e. the best interests of women and children victims of violence that occur in the domestic and/or public sphere; and

f. to provide certainty of assistance to the victim in the legal process against perpetrators of violence against women and children.

Article 21

Forms of services for victims provided by UPTD PPA include:

a. medical services;
b. medicolegal services (visum);
c. psychosocial services;
d. legal services;
e. economic independence services; and
f. spiritual services.

